    98	`\sqrt{I:B^\infty}=I(V_{X_0}(I))`, which is load-bearing for the definition, for step 2.4/2.5, for
    99	step 4.6's `e_Q=\operatorname{HF}(\mathbf1)`, and hence for rows
   100	`C-NEW-QN-PRODUCT-SPAN-DEFECT` and `C-NEW-QN-HILBERT-VANISH-ENTANGLEMENT`. Under the r1 brief's
   101	rule ("fabricated FATAL for the dependent row") this is FATAL for that definition and those rows.
