   168	### O25 — MINOR — the copy-residual defining equation is off by a conjugation, against C3
   169	
   170	**Location.** `D-QN-COPY-RESIDUAL-OBSERVABLE`, "let `|F_j\rangle\in\operatorname{Sym}^m(\mathcal H)`
   171	satisfy, under C3, `f_j(\overline\psi)=\langle F_j|\psi^{\otimes m}\rangle`"; the same equation in
   172	`C-NEW-QN-COPY-RESIDUAL`; the corresponding line in "What the seed can estimate from copies".
   173	
   174	**Computation.** With `|F\rangle` the C-019 tensor of a degree-`m` form
   175	(`|F\rangle=\sum_\alpha f_\alpha(\alpha!/m!)\sum_{{\rm content}(w)=\alpha}|w\rangle`), a direct
   176	computation gives `\langle F|\psi^{\otimes m}\rangle=\sum_\alpha\overline{f_\alpha}\psi^\alpha
   177	=\overline{f(\overline\psi)}`. Numerically (`q=2, n=3, m=2`, random complex form and state):
   178	`\langle F|\psi^{\otimes 2}\rangle = 0.1092567019+0.6211036221i`, `f(\overline\psi) =
   179	0.1092567019-0.6211036221i`, so the identity holds against `\overline{f(\overline\psi)}` and fails
   180	against `f(\overline\psi)`. The same run confirms `\|F\|=\|f\|_{\rm BW}` to `1e-15` and
   181	`\|\sum_j w_j|F_j\rangle\langle F_j|\|\le\Lambda` (so `0\le A_F\le\mathbb1` is correct).
   182	
   183	**FIX DEMAND.** Write either `\overline{f_j(\overline\psi)}=\langle F_j|\psi^{\otimes m}\rangle`
   184	with `|F_j\rangle` the C-019 tensor, or keep the displayed equation and say that `|F_j\rangle` is the
   185	*conjugate* of the C-019 tensor (its BW norm is unchanged, so `\|F_j\|=\|f_j\|_{\rm BW}` survives
   186	either way). Same edit in the row and in the prose.
   187	
   188	**SURVIVING STATEMENT.** `\langle\psi|^{\otimes m}A_F|\psi\rangle^{\otimes m}
   189	=\Lambda^{-1}\sum_j w_j|f_j(\overline\psi)|^2` is correct under either convention, because only the
   190	modulus enters; `\Lambda=\sum_j w_j\|F_j\|^2` does give `0\le A_F\le\mathbb 1`.
